## Hint Issue: Form misleads day-first users

**34 reports** from ticket #4471

Booking form v3 shows "MM/DD/YYYY" hint to all users, but users in day-first locales (de-DE, es-ES, pt-PT) naturally type DD/MM, causing misinterpretation.

<Callout>
Root cause identified. Fix queued. GitHub issue: #12
</Callout>

### How it fails

- User in Germany sees booking form with hint "MM/DD/YYYY"
- User naturally types "12/3" (meaning March 12 in German convention DD/MM)
- User assumes the hint is just informational; they type their own way
- Form interprets "12/3" according to the hint: December 3
- Date is wrong

### Affected tenants

- alder.physio (de-DE, booking-v3): 12 reports
- copper.studio (es-ES, booking-v3): 11 reports
- pale.harbour (pt-PT, booking-v3): 11 reports

### Affected channel

Form-based bookings only (booking-v3)

### Root cause

Form hint is hardcoded to MM/DD regardless of user locale.

### Fix approach

1. Detect user's locale dynamically
2. Show locale-appropriate hint: "DD/MM/YYYY" for day-first, "MM/DD/YYYY" for month-first
3. Parse input according to the hint shown

### GitHub issue

[#12: Hint issue (34 reports) — form misleads day-first users](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/12)

